@page
@using VeskaFlow.Web.Services
@inject IConfiguration Config
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of Service";
    var operatorName = LegalInfo.OperatorName(Config);
    var contact = LegalInfo.ContactText(Config);
}
<div class="card legal">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="muted">Version @LegalInfo.Version</p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>VeskaFlow, run by @operatorName, lets a barbershop, salon, clinic or other appointment-based business take online bookings, manage its day, and keep simple customer and follow-up records. By creating a shop you agree to these Terms and to the <a href="/Privacy">Privacy Notice</a>. You must be at least 18 and able to enter a contract for the business.</p>

    <h2>Free trial and fees</h2>
    <p>A new shop gets a free trial (30 days unless we say otherwise). When it ends, online booking closes and the back office is locked until the shop subscribes; nothing is deleted at that point.</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Price and how to pay:</strong> the subscription price and the payment details are shown in the app (About page and the trial-ended page). The subscription is paid in advance for the period you choose, for now by GCash to @operatorName; it is not charged automatically.</li>
        <li><strong>Starting and renewing:</strong> your access is extended once we see your payment. Send proof of payment with your shop name and the email you sign in with.</li>
        <li><strong>Add-ons:</strong> some extras, such as more customer emails per day or the AI assistant on your booking page, are paid separately for the period you choose; the price is shown in the app and they are paid and renewed like the subscription. Without the email add-on the number of emails the system sends for you each day is limited. The AI assistant stays off until we switch it on for your shop after payment.</li>
        <li><strong>Refunds:</strong> fees are paid for a period of access and are not refundable once that period has started, unless the law requires otherwise or we agree in writing.</li>
        <li><strong>Price changes:</strong> we tell you by email at least 30 days before a price change takes effect for you.</li>
        <li><strong>Not paying:</strong> if access ends and is not renewed, the shop stays locked. We keep its data as described in the Privacy Notice and tell you by email before deleting an inactive shop.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>You must confirm your email address. Keep your password private: you are responsible for what is done with your account and for the people you let in as managers or staff. Tell us if you think someone else has access. We send notices about your account to your confirmed email address.</p>

    <h2>What you may and may not do</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Use the service only for your own business, lawfully.</li>
        <li>Do not use it to send spam, to collect data you have no right to, or to attack or overload the system.</li>
        <li>Do not enter data about people who have not been told that the shop keeps it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your customers' data (data processing)</h2>
    <p>Your shop is the personal information controller of its customers' data; @operatorName is your processor under the Data Privacy Act of 2012. That means:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>@operatorName processes that data only to provide the service and on your instructions, and keeps it confidential.</li>
        <li><strong>You</strong> are responsible for having a lawful basis and, where needed, the customer's consent (and a parent's or guardian's for a child). For health information (a clinic's visit notes) you are responsible for getting the patient's consent and for keeping the notes to what you need.</li>
        <li>We keep the data secure as described in the Privacy Notice, use the service providers listed there, and tell you without undue delay if we learn of a breach that affects your shop.</li>
        <li>You can export or delete any customer's data in the app, which is how a customer's request to see or erase their data can be met. We help with such requests if you ask.</li>
        <li>When your shop is deleted, we delete its data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Health records</h2>
    <p>The visit notes and follow-ups are simple notes for your own use. VeskaFlow is not a certified electronic medical records system and does not replace the records, licences or rules that apply to your profession. You remain responsible for meeting them.</p>

    <h2>AI assistant (optional add-on)</h2>
    <p>If the AI assistant is switched on for your shop, customers can chat on your booking page and book through it. Its replies are written automatically by an AI service and can be wrong, so:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>It answers only about your services, prices and free times, and can make only a booking the customer asks for, under the same rules as the booking form. It cannot cancel or move a booking. You and the customer can check a booking made in the chat like any other, and you can cancel it.</li>
        <li>It is not a person and not a professional. Do not use it, or let customers use it, for medical or other advice.</li>
        <li>The chat tells customers that it is an automated assistant and links to the Privacy Notice. Do not hide or remove that. You remain responsible, as the controller, for your customers' data.</li>
        <li>Chats are kept for 30 days and then deleted (see the Privacy Notice). The AI service provider listed there processes the messages for us.</li>
        <li>Each shop has a monthly number of chats. If it is reached, or the AI service is unavailable, the chat pauses and the booking form keeps working. We do not promise that the assistant is available at all times.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Ownership</h2>
    <p>You keep all rights to your shop's data. @operatorName keeps all rights to the VeskaFlow software, name and design; you get the right to use the service while your access lasts. Do not copy, resell or reverse engineer it.</p>

    <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>We work to keep the service running, but it is provided as it is. It may be down for maintenance or for reasons outside our control, and we do not promise it will be uninterrupted or error-free. We make nightly backups, but keep your own record of anything you cannot afford to lose; you can export your customers from the app. We may change or remove features; we will tell you of a change that matters.</p>

    <h2>Suspension and ending</h2>
    <p>We may switch a shop off if these Terms are broken or the service is being abused. You can stop using the service at any time and ask us to delete your shop. Deleting a shop deletes all of its data permanently.</p>

    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>To the extent the law allows, @operatorName is not liable for lost income, lost bookings or indirect damage arising from use of the service, and its total liability is limited to the fees you paid in the 3 months before the claim.</p>

    <h2>Law and contact</h2>
    <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the Philippines. Questions: @contact. These Terms are a plain description of the arrangement and are not legal advice.</p>
</div>
